  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "dxf_entities_read",
    "file": "libredwg/src/in_dxf.c",
    "description": "In dxf_entities_read, a heap string dxfname is allocated with strdup and passed to new_object(), which stores it in the created object's obj->dxfname for later cleanup by dwg_free/free_preR13_object. On the error path when new_object() returns NULL, dxf_entities_read also calls free(dxfname) but does not clear the already-stored obj->dxfname pointer. Later dwg_free() frees obj->dxfname again (FREE_IF in free_preR13_object), causing a double-free. The bug is ownership/lifetime mismanagement in dxf_entities_read's failure handling, not in free_preR13_object.",
    "conditions": "Trigger requires DXF input parsed by llvmfuzz via dwg_read_dxf into dxf_entities_read, with an entity name causing dxfname=strdup(pair->value.s), then a malformed/partial entity such that new_object(name,dxfname,...) fails and returns NULL after object creation/assignment of dxfname. dxf_entities_read frees dxfname immediately and returns DWG_ERR_INVALIDDWG; harness then calls dwg_free(&dwg), which traverses partially built objects and frees obj->dxfname again, producing the ASan double-free."
  },
